 ### [Multi-view Consistency Supervision](16585-multi-view-consistency-supervision.md)
-A supervision signal that ensures semantic consistency (e.g., road lanes look consistent from any view) by generating rays from unseen views and supervising their color against pseudo-ground truth, weighted by a confidence function. It differs from standard depth supervision by focusing on semantic consistency across views rather than just geometric depth accuracy [G]. Choose this for driving scenes or structured environments where semantic priors (like map data) are available. Link: [MapNeRF](mapnerf.md).
