 ## Background
-Generalized Ray Supervision was introduced in ShadowNeuS (2023) as a generalization of the NeRF training paradigm, revealing that NeRF essentially supervises camera rays and that this can be extended to arbitrary rays like shadow rays [S1]. It was further developed in MapNeRF (2023) to incorporate map priors for driving view simulation, using multi-view consistency supervision to enforce semantic consistency . The method builds on the differentiable volume rendering framework established by NeRF [G].
